Subphase 2.1: Configurable clipping and compatibility raster state
  Dependencies: completed Phases 1–2 and existing categorized StateCache/engine-boundary foundation.
  Authorization: user requested this subphase after approving support for the settings previously
  represented by fixed RasterizerDesc properties. Implementation completed 2026-10-06.
  Outcome: these settings are configurable complete-pipeline state, with explicit defaults, validated
  capabilities, cache-backed application and faithful engine-boundary restoration.
  Sources: Rendering.AuthoritativePipelineState.Proposal.md / Static and dynamic state coverage;
  Rendering.AuthoritativePipelineState.md / Supported state and defaults, Immutable graphics descriptions;
  RasterizerDesc, PipelineCanonicalization, PipelineFixedFunctionValidation and existing boundary coverage.
  Contract amendment: supersede the initial exclusions for user clip distances, alternate clip origin/depth
  conventions, alpha test, point/line/polygon smoothing, line/polygon stipple and point-sprite origin.
  Preserve current fixed values as construction defaults and explicit first-consumer choices, not restrictions.
  Other exclusions (including logic operations, viewport arrays and fixed-function lighting) remain unchanged.
  This subphase brings forward only the application/restoration work needed for these settings; it does
  not complete Phase 3's general application, instrumentation or consumer-boundary acceptance gates.

  Evidence: Rendering.AuthoritativePipelineState.md / Configurable raster state contract.
  Completed after second source review and independent audit-stage-completion: no unresolved findings.
  Shader-enabled Debug/Release runtime selection: 124/124 each, zero failures/skips;
  original generator suites: 177/177 each. Approved metadata-removal correction validated runtime
  124/124 and generator 173/173 in both configurations, zero failures/skips; compiler-derived output
  checks remain Phase 4 prerequisites. Native core and compatibility coverage; unavailable clip-control
  rejection is synthetic-only. Live-game appearance and performance were not evaluated.

