Phase 2.2: Correct native error polling and checked-operation ownership
  Dependencies: Phases 1–2 and Subphase 2.1; existing engine-boundary restoration foundation.
  Outcome: ordinary cached transitions avoid unconditional native error polling, while checked
  boundaries and pixel transfers retain explicit failure and safe-restoration guarantees.
  Scope: corrective error-checking policy within existing StateCache owners; no PSO identity,
  capability-model, renderer-side state-management or context-lifetime redesign.

  ☐ Reconcile the proposal and implementation contract before changing polling behavior.
    ☐ Distinguish managed input/capability validation, optional per-command diagnostics and required
      checked operations. Ordinary transitions do not promise immediate detection of every native error.
    ☐ Define responsibility for pre-existing errors, post-operation checks and cache publication;
      retain failed-query rejection and prevent unsafe handoff from being reported as successful.
    ☐ Inventory nested checks in rasterizer setters, restoration, pack/unpack layouts, pixel-buffer
      bindings and polygon-stipple transfers; identify every required check and its owning operation.
  ☐ Correct ordinary transitions and unchanged-state paths through existing cache APIs.
    ☐ Remove unconditional native error polling from ordinary rasterizer transitions; preserve managed
      validation, per-field knowledge, external invalidation and necessary native state changes.
    ☐ Return from known unchanged pack/unpack layout updates without native calls or error polling.
    ☐ Make detailed per-command checking explicitly optional through existing diagnostic ownership;
      normal execution must not accidentally retain the same polling cost through nested helpers.
  ☐ Consolidate required checks at explicit operation boundaries.
    ☐ Avoid duplicate outer/inner checks during restoration while attempting independent restores
      after a failure and preserving operation plus cleanup exceptions.
    ☐ Define checked-group granularity and invalidate all affected knowledge when a group fails;
      do not claim exact per-field failure attribution from a batch-level error result.
    ☐ Preserve verified pixel-buffer binding/layout setup before host-pointer transfers, borrowed
      pack/unpack state restoration and propagation of unsafe restoration failures.
    ☐ Keep checks required by cold queries and native safety; do not replace targeted invalidation
      with blanket cache invalidation or consume errors on ordinary unchanged transitions.
  ☐ Delegate focused verification in shader-enabled Debug and Release.
    ☐ Assert zero native error polling for ordinary changed and unchanged transitions with detailed
      diagnostics disabled; separately verify optional diagnostics and required checked operations.
    ☐ Replace tests that require redundant polling, including unchanged boundary restoration counts,
      with assertions matching the documented check ownership and native mutation suppression.
    ☐ Retain real native-failure, failed-query, hostile incoming state, independent cleanup, exception
      aggregation and pixel-transfer safety tests; verify native state and cache knowledge agree.
    ☐ Record state mutations, value queries and error checks separately; update implementation
      evidence with fresh receipts. Reduced call counts alone do not establish frame-time savings.
  ☐ Completion gate: proposal, plan and implementation contracts agree; focused verification,
    second source review and independent completion audit find no unresolved failure-contract gaps.

